 "response": "An implementation of the `Poll` class meeting all requirements:\n\n```python\nclass Poll:\n    def __init__(self, question: str) -> None:\n        self.question = question\n        self.options: list[str] = []\n        self.votes: dict[str, str] = {}\n\n    def add_option(self, option: str) -> None:\n        if option not in self.options:\n            self.options.append(option)\n\n    def vote(self, voter: str, option: str) -> None:\n        if option not in self.options:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Option '{option}' does not exist.\")\n        self.votes[voter] = option\n\n    def winner(self) -> str | None:\n        if len(self.votes) < 3:\n            return None\n\n        counts = {opt: 0 for opt in self.options}\n        for opt in self.votes.values():\n            counts[opt] += 1\n\n        max_votes = max(counts.values())\n\n        # In case of a tie, the option added last wins\n        for opt in reversed(self.options):\n            if counts[opt] == max_votes:\n                return opt\n\n        return None\n```",
